{"id": "swh-0001", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Habari gani?", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "How are you? / What's new?", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The real greeting. Not a question — it is the opener in every short encounter.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0001", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": "Greet before asking anything. Skipping the greeting to go straight to a question reads as rude even when the Swahili is perfect.", "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0002", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Nzuri", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Fine / Good", "register": "neutral", "direction": "understand", "why": "The expected reply to Habari gani. One word, and it invites the greeting to continue.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0001", "exchange_turn": 2, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0003", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Poa", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Fine / Okay", "register": "informal", "direction": "understand", "why": "The other standard reply. Slightly more casual than Nzuri and very common.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0004", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Hujambo", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "No trouble (a greeting)", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The fuller form of the greeting, and the traditional one. Also works as a reply to Habari gani.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0002", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0005", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Jambo", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Hello", "register": "informal", "direction": "say", "why": "The shortened form, and the one travellers are taught. Universally understood, so it is the safe default if you are unsure.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": "It is a simplification used mostly with foreigners. A local greets with Habari, not Jambo — so it is understood, but it marks you as a learner.", "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0006", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Habari za asubuhi", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Good morning", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Morning greeting, built on Habari. Note the za — the greeting takes a plural class marker here.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0007", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Habari za mchana", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Good afternoon", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Afternoon greeting.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0008", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Habari za jioni", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Good evening", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Evening greeting.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0009", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Siku nzuri", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Have a good day", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The standard warm farewell. Spelled with 'kiku', not 'chiku' — the aspirated p is written k.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": "The spelling matters. 'Siku' with the aspirated k is the only correct form; the English-influenced 'siku/chiku' is a very common learner error.", "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0010", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Karibu", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Welcome / You are welcome", "register": "neutral", "direction": "understand", "why": "Both the reply to a greeting and the reply to thanks. Note that asante is for thanks and karibu is for welcome — mixing them is a common error.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0002", "exchange_turn": 2, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0011", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Asante", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Thank you", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The highest-frequency courtesy phrase. Used for both a gift and a service, unlike many languages.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0004", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0012", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Asante sana", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Thank you very much", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Stronger than plain Asante. Sana is the general intensifier and costs nothing to add.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0013", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Tafadhali", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Please", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Goes AFTER the request in Swahili, unlike English and unlike most of this catalogue.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0003", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": "Position is the whole trick. 'Tafadhali' in front of a request is not wrong exactly, but placing it at the end is what a local does.", "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0014", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Pole", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Sorry", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The everyday apology — bumping into someone, interrupting yourself. Single word, very high frequency.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0005", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0015", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Kwaheri", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Goodbye", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Neutral farewell to anyone.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0016", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Tutaonana", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "See you", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Warmer than Kwaheri. Also the stem of tutaonana kesho, see you tomorrow.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0017", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Jina langu ni", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "My name is", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The introduction half of meeting anyone. Incomplete alone — always attach a name.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0007", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0018", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Jina lako ni nani?", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "What is your name?", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The other half of an introduction. Needs almost no vocabulary to be useful.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0007", "exchange_turn": 2, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0019", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Ninatoka India", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I come from India", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Answers the question you will be asked most. The country alone is enough.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0020", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Habari za familia?", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "How is the family?", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The warmest ordinary follow-up after the greeting. People answer it, and it opens a conversation rather than closing one.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0001", "exchange_turn": 3, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0021", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Naomba", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Excuse me / I ask", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Getting someone's attention politely, and a softener that makes any request less abrupt.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0003", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0022", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Hapa", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Here", "register": "neutral", "direction": "understand", "why": "One half of the single most common location question. You will hear it constantly.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0023", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Kule", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "There / over there", "register": "neutral", "direction": "understand", "why": "The other half. Paired with Hapa it answers where something is.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0024", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Nini?", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "What?", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "One syllable, and it works with anything you cannot yet name. Points at a thing and asks.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0025", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Ndiyo", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Yes", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Standard agreement. Note it is two syllables and is also used to mean 'it is'.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0026", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Hapana", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "No", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Standard refusal, and softer than a bare 'no' would be in most contexts.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0027", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Ndiyo, kabisa", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Yes, of course", "register": "neutral", "direction": "understand", "why": "The reply you will hear most when you ask for something small. Kabisa means 'especially' or 'indeed'.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0028", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 1, "text_native": "Sana", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Very", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The general intensifier, and it goes AFTER the word it modifies. Worth learning early because it multiplies whatever you already know.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": "Postpositive. 'Sana asante' is correct; 'asante sana' is the set phrase exception you learn as a unit.", "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0029", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Sielewi", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I don't understand", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The most useful repair phrase in the language. One word, and it keeps the interaction alive.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0006", "exchange_turn": 2, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0030", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Sikuelewi", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I don't understand you", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The same idea addressed at the person rather than the language. Slightly more direct and slightly more useful.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0031", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Tena", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Again", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "One word that asks for a repeat. Works anywhere, needs no sentence around it.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0032", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Polepole", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Slowly / gently", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Asking someone to slow down is more effective than asking them to repeat, because it gives them something to actually change.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0006", "exchange_turn": 3, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0033", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Sema polepole, tafadhali", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Speak slowly, please", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The full form of the most valuable repair phrase in the language.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0034", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Unaweza kurudisha?", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Can you repeat it?", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Polite repeat request. Note tafadhali usually goes at the end even here.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0035", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Nisaidie", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Help me", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Works when you have no words for the problem at all, which is most of the time early on.", "exchange_id": "swh-x0008", "exchange_turn": 1, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0036", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Nimefika", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I have arrived", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The arrival formula. The 'nime-' prefix carries tense and completion; you cannot say it about anything else.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0037", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Nimepitika", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I am lost", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "'Nime-' plus 'pitika', to get lost. The single most useful phrase when you have no other vocabulary and are on foot.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0038", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Siwezi", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I cannot", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The negative form, and a first item in the negative tense because it is irregular: si- plus -wezi.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0039", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Sijui", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I don't know", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Honest, short, and keeps an interaction moving instead of stalling it. Also irregular like Siwezi.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0040", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Hakuna matata", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "No problem / You're welcome", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Two things at once: the reply to thanks, and a way to release yourself from a small awkwardness.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0041", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Ninasikitika", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "I am sorry (for something that happened)", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "The fuller apology, distinct from Pole. Pole covers the everyday bump; this is for an actual mistake.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
{"id": "swh-0042", "lang": "swh", "tier": 0, "domain": 12, "text_native": "Tafadhali tafsiri", "text_romanized": null, "text_english": "Please translate", "register": "neutral", "direction": "say", "why": "Points at any written thing and works without needing to read it. Useful even though this app has no reading goal, because the sign is in front of you.", "exchange_id": null, "exchange_turn": null, "caution": null, "source": {"class": "authored", "id": "LangKraft editorial", "url": null, "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "external_id": null}, "failure_flags": []}
